 this up three different times  in season 7 episode 6  which was the episode right before john  and danny had sex  when jon went out beyond the wall to  capture a white he wanted to give  longclaw back to jorah mormont so that  it could stay in his family  but as you all know jorah would not  accept the sword  he told jon to keep it he said it will  serve you well  and your children after you i've  forfeited the right to claim this song  it's yours it'd serve you well  and your children after you  you could see that john actually  considered what he said  john was always concerned about having  any children because he did not want  them to grow up as a bastard like he did  but for the first time in the show we  see john think about that possibility  this made me wonder if jon did have any  children  who would he have them with it did seem  like danny would be the obvious answer  if anyone at all  however later in this same episode we  are reminded that danny cannot have any  children  this happens when daenerys and tyrion  are having a conversation about  succession  on dragonstone tyrion is worried about  what would happen to westeros after dany  died  after you break the wheel how do we make  sure it stays broken  you want to know who sits on the iron  throne after i'm dead  is that it you say you can't have  children  but there are other ways of choosing a  successor he thinks it would just go  back to the way it has always been  now these scenes about john and danny  having children may not seem like  anything right now  but this is brought up again and again  in this same season  at the end of this episode after dany's  dragon dies  we hear her mention this to jon she says  the dragons are the only children she'll  ever have  [Music]  the dragons are my children  they're the only children i'll ever have  do you understand  this is when it became obvious that john  and danny were starting to fall for each  other  so it was very interesting that this  continued t